# Semantic HTML

Prefer semantic elements over generic `<div>` and `<span>` wrappers.

## Common Mappings

| Use case | ✅ Semantic | ❌ Avoid |
|---|---|---|
| Page sections | `<header>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`, `<aside>` | `<div id="header">` |
| Navigation | `<nav>` | `<div class="nav">` |
| Article/blog content | `<article>` | `<div class="post">` |
| Grouped content | `<section>` | `<div class="section">` |
| Buttons | `<button>` | `<div onClick>` |
| Links | `<a href="...">` | `<span onClick>` |
| Lists | `<ul>`, `<ol>`, `<li>` | `<div class="list">` |
| Images with captions | `<figure>` + `<figcaption>` | `<div class="image">` |
| Inline emphasis | `<strong>`, `<em>` | `<span class="bold">` |
| Forms | `<form>`, `<label>`, `<fieldset>` | bare `<div>` wrappers |
| Time/dates | `<time datetime="...">` | `<span>` |

## Examples

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<div class="header">
  <div class="nav">
    <div onclick="go('/')">Home</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<header>
  <nav>
    <a href="/">Home</a>
  </nav>
</header>
```

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<div class="post">
  <div class="title">My Post</div>
  <div class="content">...</div>
</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<article>
  <h1>My Post</h1>
  <p>...</p>
</article>
```
